Our platform team is building a defensive security test suite for an internal lab inventory service. It will run in CI against our own staging copy before the next internal review, and I need the test plan for it first. Nobody had time to write a threat write-up or any API documentation, so all I have are the routes as they are today (Postgres behind it, JWT auth, roles are `staff` and `admin`):

```
POST /auth/login            {email, password} -> {accessToken (JWT, 15 min), refreshToken}
POST /auth/refresh          {refreshToken}
GET  /labs/:labId/loans?from=&to=&note=
POST /transfers             {fromLabId, toLabId, assetId, quantity, note}
GET  /admin/users?search=
POST /admin/users/:id/deactivate
```

Staff members manage several labs each. Admins can see everything. The note filter and the admin search are both passed into Postgres queries. Please write up what we should test, organised so my team can start working through it.

Can you turn this into a set of security tests for our infra? We deploy with CDK and I'm not very confident in it.

